\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{When two coupling products admit conjugation}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{The [onsite Yukawa operator](fdip-011M) acts by a supplied
linear map on the fermion fiber. With two labeled couplings into
the same space, which information survives independent changes of
coordinates in their sources? Can a trace distinguish their
products from their conjugates?}

\p{If all the traces agree, which charge conjugation on the
multiplicity space can be used with the finite inversion of
\ref{fdip-013T}? When can both products be written with real
entries in a common orthonormal basis?}

